Patches applied on top of the pristine upstream tarball by
scripts/vendor-webrtc-apm.sh, in filename order.

The upstream patches/ directory of webrtc-audio-processing (MinGW fixes,
MSVC winsock2/XMM fixes, BSD support) is a record of deltas that are already
applied in the v2.1 release tree. Verified against v2.1:
rtc_base/system/file_wrapper.cc and rtc_base/logging.cc already include
<windows.h> in lower case with <winsock2.h> first, and
rtc_base/platform_thread_types.cc already guards the structured-exception
thread naming with #ifndef __MINGW32__.

Local patches:

- `0001-trace-event-include-cstdint.patch` makes `trace_event.h` self-contained.
  GCC 15.2/MinGW does not obtain the global `uint8_t` typedef transitively
  through `<string>`, so the unpatched header fails native Windows builds.
